 61V 4c  of {+61}V                                                              
 61V  c  2003So02: {+61}V produced in fragmentation of {+76}Ge{+30+} beam on    
 61V 2c  {+58}Ni target. LISE3 achromatic spectrometer used to separate         
 61V 3c  fragments; measured half-life of {+61}V decay and probability of       
 61V 4c  delayed-neutron decay from the observation of 2+ to 0+ transition in   
 61V 5c  {+60}Cr.                                                               
 61V  c  2011Da08 (also 2002MaZN thesis): {+61}Ti produced in the fragmentation 
 61V 2c  of 57.8 MeV/nucleon {+86}Kr beam impinged on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick        
 61V 3c  tantalum target using LISE-2000 spectrometer at GANIL facility.        
 61V 4c  Detector system included a three-element Si-detector telescope         
